# Only src/, VERSION, BUILD and LICENSE ever enter the image (see the Dockerfile's COPY
# lines); everything else here would still be sent to the Docker daemon, or a remote
# builder, as part of the build context whether or not any instruction ever reads it.
# `config/` in particular is runtime state that can hold real Sonarr API keys and
# session data — it has no business leaving the host at all, build or otherwise.

.git/
.venv/
.vscode/
.idea/

docs/
tests/
tools/

# Runtime state: settings, sessions, journals, caches, posters, logs.
config/
data/
state/
runtime/
*.log
*.log.*

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

node_modules/

*.bak
*.backup
*.tmp
*.temp
*.orig
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
